Release operator states when a prepared statement's execution ends

A prepared plan outlives its executions (a statement cache, an explicit
prepared statement), and its operators keep the last execution's global sink
and operator states until the plan is executed again or destroyed: a hash
table, a sort, or the states of an aggregate. For a C-API aggregate whose
states are Python objects, those objects then stay alive after the query
finished, and a state that refers back to the client keeps it alive too. Drop
the states when the statement ends, after its executor (and result collector)
is gone, following EXECUTE into the prepared plan it runs.

